      ",", "\"\<HRF_HyperCrownCodimensionSurvey.wl\>\""}], "}"}], "]"}], 
   "]"}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"hrfHyperCrownCodimensionSurveyTable", "[", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[10a]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1d66b9c6-0b9e-4075-a3c6-d822e2af12f3"],

Cell["Exact graph symmetry and orbit completion", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"228ca0f6-181e-4b36-b6c7-9e4f8498bbfc"],

Cell["\<\
The HyperCrown graph has the D4 automorphism group of its four-edge square. \
Some elements leave s12 and s23 fixed; others exchange them. In this topology \
survey an external permutation, its induced edge permutation and the \
corresponding relabelling of the two invariants are performed together. A \
crossing-related image is therefore the same physical case with a different \
choice of which symmetric external pair is called incoming. The positive \
Schwinger orthant, cancellation locus and region vector are carried \
bijectively to the image, so one HRF representative certifies its full D4 \
orbit.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c6ad60b3-b2f2-4a6c-ac05-9bbd578bac85"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"hrfHyperCrownSymmetryAudit", "[", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[10b]:=",ExpressionUUID->"483922c6-3b14-45b1-9184-c0a2b7638e96"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"hrfHyperCrownSymmetryOrbitTable", "[", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[10c]:=",ExpressionUUID->"60c8ab3d-1d32-4b87-b4ce-3b62a247c53f"],

Cell["Enumeration and level of certainty", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"cc46a69e-ac7e-4e44-b0b3-83d2f0a1cecf"],

Cell["\<\
There are two inequivalent HyperCrown boundary-HR types through codimension \
two. Type I has one square edge contracted and four labelled representatives. \
Type II has two adjacent square edges contracted and four labelled \
representatives. The opposite-edge orbit has no HR: on x8=x9=0 the complete \
uncapped polynomial-factor construction produces only the s12-supported \
Crown-like generator, while the s23 coefficient supplies no companion \
generator; exact coverage proves that the remaining one-generator \
presentation has no scaling vector. The x10=x11 result follows by D4 \
symmetry. The interior remains a separate unresolved search.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"80ca4a5b-a86e-4a23-9efc-93d176f142d1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"hrfHyperCrownEstablishedTypeTable", "[", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[10d]:=",ExpressionUUID->"efbaca35-4c7b-4f15-8237-6913c8d6baef"],

Cell["\<\
Notation is kept separate: B denotes equations x_e=0, whereas v_e is a \
component of the scaling vector defined by x_e~delta^(v_e). The master edge \
order is X=(x0,x1,...,x11); delete the variables in B while retaining that \
order. Every augmented normal is displayed horizontally as v_B=(v_e;1), \
followed by named component rules {v_i->...}. The two accepted generator \
presentations on each directly positive codimension-two stratum give the same \
vector, so they constitute one region rather than two distinct HRs.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b56f384f-0318-4aa1-92b3-0e75aa48388e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"hrfHyperCrownPositiveRegionVectorTable", "[", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[10e]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a38da29f-1d7f-45d8-a2c1-397e0bc37b52"],

Cell["\<\
Search budgets are explicit. The exploratory profile is useful for finding \
positive witnesses; it cannot certify absence. The certified profile removes \
the candidate, two-generator-union and polynomial-size caps. \
FullHarvestQ->True means complete factorisation of the relevant derivatives \
and primitive channel polynomials. The former signed-monomial-pair \
enlargement is retained only as a legacy diagnostic because arbitrary \
two-term sub-sums are not polynomial cancellation factors.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4bea0c7b-b4f0-4249-8da7-6f05092cbcf2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Dataset", "[", 
  RowBox[{"KeyValueMap", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"name", ",", "cfg"}], "}"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
       RowBox[{
